\section{The sample/time boundary (D-8)}{

One rule governs the whole data layer: the integer \strong{sample index} is the
canonical key for storage, computation, and joins, while \strong{time (seconds)}
is the presentation unit. The conversion is exact and free
(\code{time = sample / frequency}). User-facing arguments speak seconds;
internal work happens in samples; results carry both. See \code{\link[=time_to_sample]{time_to_sample()}}
and \code{\link[=sample_to_time]{sample_to_time()}}.
}

